    {
      "block_id": 0,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "STATE 12 \nThe write portion of the cycle starts in S 12. The valid function codes on \nFC2-FCO, the address bus lines, AS, and R/W remain unaltered. \n",
      "bbox": [
        48.720001220703125,
        47.75000762939453,
        433.3505859375,
        72.2304458618164
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.09666666908869667,
        0.07357927455107005,
        0.8598225911458334,
        0.11130184204915448
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 1,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "STATE 13 \nDuring S13, no bus signals are altered. \n",
      "bbox": [
        48.959999084472656,
        79.92005157470703,
        273.97906494140625,
        93.1104507446289
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.09714285532633464,
        0.12315096287714691,
        0.5436092558361235,
        0.14347640469685524
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 2,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "STATE 14 \nOn the rising edge of S14, the processor drives R/W low. \n",
      "bbox": [
        48.720001220703125,
        100.79999542236328,
        349.767822265625,
        113.99039459228516
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.09666666908869667,
        0.15532543147412933,
        0.6939837743365576,
        0.17565087329383766
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 3,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "STATE 15 \nDuring S15, the data bus is driven out of the high-impedance state as the \ndata to be written are placed on the bus. \n",
      "bbox": [
        48.959999084472656,
        121.92005157470703,
        433.9477844238281,
        146.3904266357422
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.09714285532633464,
        0.18786989559711909,
        0.8610075087774367,
        0.22557695648301476
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 4,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "STATE 16 At the rising edge of S 16, the processor asserts Uos or [OS. The \n",
      "bbox": [
        48.959999084472656,
        152.5750274658203,
        435.54290771484375,
        167.68902587890625
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.09714285532633464,
        0.23510697469781738,
        0.8641724359421503,
        0.25839654246987154
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 5,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "processor waits for DTACK or BEAR or VPA, an M6800 peripheral signal. \nWhen VPA is asserted during S16, the cycle becomes a peripheral cycle \n",
      "bbox": [
        106.64999389648438,
        165.35000610351562,
        434.6691589355469,
        189.59043884277344
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.2116071307469928,
        0.25479228381572416,
        0.8624388074117993,
        0.2921450203765584
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 6,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "(refer to Appendix B M6800 Peripheral Interface). If neither termination \nsignal is asserted before the falling edge at the close of S 16, the processor \ninserts wait states (full clock cycles) until either DTACK or BEAR is asserted. \n",
      "bbox": [
        106.83999633789062,
        187.68002319335938,
        434.4820556640625,
        222.95042419433594
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.21198411971803696,
